# doc spec

This file defines the syntax and formatting rules of xLaDe.
Please follow this format only while creating a new documentation file.

---

## File format

- file should use extensionless format
- no capitalization unless some standard or special file needs capital format (such as LICENSE)
- use underscore "_" to separate words
- do not include custom non utf-8 characters in filenames

---

## Headings

- Beginning of document starts with single # symbol telling the file name 
- Headings are ##
- Subheadings are ###
- Subsubheadings are #### and so on

---

## Comments

- Single line comments use //
- Multiline comments start with //-- and end with --//
- No need to put multiline comment symbols in every line, just starting and ending is sufficient

---

## Lists

- Use "-" for unordered list
- Use "1." and similar for ordered list
- There should be a single space after the listing symbols

---

## Code

- Use backticks (``) for singleline code
- Use ``` for multiline code and first line can include language name (optional)

---

## Maths

- Tex format should be used for maths
- The equations should be enclosed with dollar symbols $

---

## Tables

- Use pipe (|) for separating columns
- The headings should be separated from rows by dashes 

---

## Quotes

- Quotes should use greater than (>) symbol
- For quotes in multilines, it should start with >- and end with -<
- Alternatively every line can use > too

---

## Normal writing

- No formatting should be used for links, references, and paragraphs
- Paragraphs should be written normally
- Links should be put directly without any custom format
- References should be written directly too without anything 

## Miscellaneous

- Use triple dashes --- between sections
- The documents should leave last line empty
- Whitespace should be exactly one line after sections. 
- No huge lines of whitespace or empty lines should be in any document
- The standard formatting of ** to bold * to italics, and ~~ to strikethrough should be minimal
- Documents may use special format based on requirements and context if rules are not adequate

---
